@node Timely Dataflow
@chapter Timely Dataflow

This chapter is a port of the timely dataflow book to C.  Where a
passage of the book relies on a Rust feature libdtfl exposes
differently, it describes the C way; where it relies on something not
yet on the pin, it says so in a sentence rather than show code that
would not compile.  Every example here is a complete C program that
compiles against the installed headers.

@menu
* Timely Motivation::           What timely dataflow is for.
* Timely Core Concepts::        A first dataflow, and a reactive one.
* Timely Dataflow Model::       Dataflow, timestamps and progress.
* Building Timely Dataflows::   Inputs, outputs and operators.
* Running Timely Dataflows::    Driving a worker.
* Advanced Timely::             Scopes, iteration, capture.
* Timely Internals::            Communication, progress, logging.
@end menu

